0.0.4fc0ec36acae796600191f045615af67b09e6afa.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:29PM MST until November 6 at 12:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a Flood Warning\nfor the following rivers in Colorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\n.Minor flooding along the Rio Grande through Alamosa is expected due\nto upstream flooding occurring in the vicinity of Monte Vista.\n\nFor the Rio Grande...including Alamosa...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon to late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 2:30 PM MST Monday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage early\nWednesday afternoon to a crest of 9.6 feet late Wednesday\nevening. It will then fall below flood stage early Thursday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-06T00:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f77eed9d842c708a5a3d2e5d0c786d35cd12c2c0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-05T01:43:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 050143 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 643 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Quick-moving disturbance to bring snow to the mountains this afternoon and evening, which will make for slick and hazardous travel. - Drier and warmer conditions starting Saturday. && .UPDATE... Issued at 642 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026 Latest high-res model trends conti","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=A